  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0250\" is used to store information about users, products, orders, and order details. It contains eight tables: User, Product, Order, User_Shopping_Cart, Admin_Product_Management, Order_Product, User_Order, and Admin_Order_Management.\nThe User table contains information about registered users, including their username, password, phone number, registration time, and role. The User_ID column is the primary key and is used to identify each user.\nThe Product table contains information about the products available for purchase, including the product name, description, price, category, and shelving time. The Product_ID column is the primary key and is used to identify each product.\nThe Order table contains information about orders placed by users, including the delivery address, order status, order time, payment time, total amount, and user ID. The Order_ID column is the primary key and is used to identify each order.\nThe User_Shopping_Cart table contains information about the products added to the shopping cart by each user, including the product ID, quantity, and user ID. The primary key is a composite key consisting of the User_ID and Product_ID columns.\nThe Admin_Product_Management table contains information about the management of products by administrators, including the admin ID, operation time, operation type, and product ID. The primary key is a composite key consisting of the Admin_ID and Product_ID columns.\nThe Order_Product table contains information about the products included in each order, including the order ID, product ID, quantity, subtotal, and unit price. The primary key is a composite key consisting of the Order_ID and Product_ID columns.\nThe User_Order table contains information about the orders placed by each user, including the delivery address, order status, order time, payment time, total amount, and user ID. The primary key is a composite key consisting of the Order_ID and User_ID columns.\nThe Admin_Order_Management table contains information about the management of orders by administrators, including the admin ID, operation time, operation type, and order ID. The primary key is a composite key consisting of the Admin_ID and Order_ID columns.\nEach table has foreign keys that reference the primary keys of other tables, ensuring referential integrity and maintaining the relationships between the tables. For example, the User_ID column in the Order table references the User_ID column in the User table, ensuring that each order is associated with a specific user. Similarly, the Product_ID column in the Order_Product table references the Product_ID column in the Product table, ensuring that each order includes specific products.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description:\n1.Frontend User Features:\nUsers can log in through the WeChat mini-program. Each user has a unique User ID, Username, Password, Phone Number, Registration Time, Last Login Time, and Role.\n2.Product Management:\nAdministrators can add, edit, and delete product information. Each product includes Product ID, Product Name, Product Description, Price, Stock Quantity, Product Category, and Shelving Time.\n3.Order Management:\nAdministrators can manage the order status, such as processing orders and shipping. Each order includes Order ID, User ID, Order Status, Total Amount, Order Time, Payment Time, and Delivery Address.\n4.Purchase Management:\nEach user can add multiple products to their shopping cart and place multiple orders, with each order containing multiple products.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0250.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0250\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Product` (\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `shelving_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Product_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Order` (\n  `Order_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `payment_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Order_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Shopping_Cart` (\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`User_ID`, `Product_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_shopping_cart_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_shopping_cart_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Product_ID`) REFERENCES `Product` (`Product_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Admin_Product_Management` (\n  `Admin_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Admin_ID`, `Product_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `admin_product_management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Admin_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `admin_product_management_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Product_ID`) REFERENCES `Product` (`Product_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Order_Product` (\n  `Order_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Product_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `subtotal` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Order_ID`, `Product_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Order_ID`) REFERENCES `Order` (`Order_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_product_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Product_ID`) REFERENCES `Product` (`Product_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Order` (\n  `Order_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `User_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `delivery_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `order_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `payment_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Order_ID`, `User_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Order_ID`) REFERENCES `Order` (`Order_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`User_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Admin_Order_Management` (\n  `Admin_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Order_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `operation_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Admin_ID`, `Order_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `admin_order_management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Admin_ID`) REFERENCES `User` (`User_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `admin_order_management_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Order_ID`) REFERENCES `Order` (`Order_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
